    <tags>ser2netweb serial serial-port com-port rs232 rs485 usb-serial tcp telnet rfc2217 udp modbus mqtt sparkplug iot serial-to-ethernet portable</tags>
    <summary>Serial-to-network bridge with a web UI: raw TCP, telnet, RFC 2217, UDP, Modbus gateway, MQTT</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[ser2netweb shares local serial ports (RS-232 / RS-485, USB adapters) over the network as raw TCP, telnet, RFC 2217 or UDP, runs a Modbus RTU/TCP gateway and publishes serial data and Modbus points to MQTT and Sparkplug B, all set up and watched in a browser, with accounts, roles, an audit log, TLS and LDAP / OpenID Connect sign-in.

ser2netweb is an independent project, unrelated to Corey Minyard's ser2net.

## Usage

* `ser2netweb` starts it in the console window; the first run asks for the web UI's address. Its data (config.json, backups, logs) is in the user's data folder, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\ser2netweb`.
* As a Windows service: `ser2netweb --install-service` from an elevated prompt. The service runs its own copy, in `C:\Program Files\ser2netweb`, with its data in `C:\ProgramData\ser2netweb`: after `choco upgrade ser2netweb`, run `ser2netweb --install-service` again to upgrade it; before `choco uninstall ser2netweb`, `ser2netweb --uninstall-service` removes it.

The package installs the release's own `ser2netweb-windows-x64.exe` (checked against its SHA-256), a single executable with everything inside (Python, OpenSSL, the VC++ runtime). Licence: AGPL-3.0-only, or a commercial licence (COMMERCIAL_LICENSE.md). Windows guide: https://github.com/haliskilic/ser2netweb/blob/main/docs/WINDOWS.md
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/haliskilic/ser2netweb/releases/tag/v3.0.0</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
